{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #236: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $f(n)$ count the number of solutions to $n=p+2^k$ for prime $p$ and $k\\geq 0$. Is it true that $f(n)=o(\\log n)$? Current best: Mientka and Weitzenkamp \\cite{MiWe69} have proved there are no other such $n\\leq 2^{44}$. Vaughan \\cite{Va73} has proved that the number of $n\\leq N$ such that $n-2^k$ is prime for all $2^k<n$ is\\[< \\exp\\left(-c\\frac{\\log \\log \\log N}{\\log\\log N}\\log N\\right)N\\]for some constant $c>0$. Prize: no. OEIS: A039669, A109925. Tags: number theory, primes."},"claim_id":"vcl_5e64c05cbe959f1ddae0b53ecbc7516e8ce2d44bb620fd56d59ada99e446d7f8","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:236","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_ea088f13ed98d3c2","object_root":"sha256:1ffa9e6fe4f2ef3ae459569dc17ca1a956af90a2f20d46e80c0face970011fe0","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:236"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,